No I understand lack of FGs in API. If this would make things easier then I'd do that, but TBH, I'm not sure we gain much. ", 'created_at': '2026-07-16T15:51:35+00:00', 'path': 'pkg/scheduler/schedule_one_podgroup.go', 'position': 395}, {'user': 'brejman', 'body': 'Updated', 'created_at': '2026-07-16T16:00:44+00:00', 'path': 'staging/src/k8s.io/api/scheduling/v1alpha3/types.go', 'position': 41}, {'user': 'mm4tt', 'body': "Let's add a comment explaining what happens here. We're returning exactly the same as in the GetPlacementCycleState method, but this is fine because those methods are from different interfaces (PGCycleState vs PlacementCycleState)?", 'created_at': '2026-07-16T16:03:57+00:00', 'path': 'pkg/scheduler/framework/cycle_state.go', 'position': 7}, {'user': 'brejman', 'body': "Technically we don't, we could just run subsequent Assumes without Forget in between. We could also remove the ForgetPlacement call in the loop below and just do
```go
parentPlacement := snapshot.GetPlacement()
defer func() {
  snapshot.ForgetPlacement()
  snapshot.AssumePlacement(parentPlacement)
}()

for _, placement := range placements {
