', 'created_at': '2026-07-20T10:37:07+00:00', 'path': 'pkg/scheduler/framework/plugins/helper/podgroup.go', 'position': 1}, {'user': 'mm4tt', 'body': "NIT: Let's structure this as a TODO. Overall, we should have a similar check at the algorithm level in `schedule_one_podgroup` to ensure this condition is satisfied whenever we call `ScorePlacement`. If it's not, we should return an error from the algorithm.", 'created_at': '2026-07-20T10:39:27+00:00', 'path': 'pkg/scheduler/framework/plugins/podgrouppodscount/podgroup_pods_count.go', 'position': 1}, {'user': 'mm4tt', 'body': 'Hmmm, this check seems dangerous now if we call `AssumePlacement(childPlacement1)` and then `AssumePlacement(childPlacement2)` without calling `ForgetPlacement` in the meantime, assuming both placements have the same number of nodes. To keep this optimization, we should actually call `ForgetPlacement` before calling `Assume` in the algorithm.', 'created_at': '2026-07-20T10:59:58+00:00', 'path': 'pkg/scheduler/backend/cache/snapshot.go', 'position': 92}, {'user': 'mm4tt', 'body': 'As pointed out in the other comment, we actually need to call it.  Here and in the compositePodGroupSchedulingPlacementAlgorithm', 'created_at': '2026-07-20T11:03:06+00:00', 'path': 'pkg/scheduler/schedule_one_podgroup.go', 'position': 144}, {'user': 'brejman', 'body': 'This optimization only checks whether the assumed placement is the same as the full set of nodes (and NOT same as the currently assumed placement), so it shouldn't matter whether we call `ForgetPlacement` or not.

